{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.WeinbergAngleCategorical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.WeinbergAngleCategorical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg_mul_cotSq_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg_mul_cotSq_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L152-L172","doc":"**Conditional consequence (§3b-cond).**  *If* the identification\nholds, the categorical `cos² θ_W` is the usual function of `cot θ_W`:\n`cos² θ_W · (cot² θ_W + 1) = cot² θ_W`.  Derived from\n`cot_identification` and `trB_ne_zero`; the only unproved input is the\nclass instance (the conjecture).  The hypothesis `cot² + 1 ≠ 0` is\nneeded because a generic field may contain `√−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.cot_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.cot_identification","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L150-L150","doc":"**The identification — the conjecture's claim.**\n`cot θ_W · tr_M(e_B⁺σ₅⁸) = tr_M(e_W⁺σ₁⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.trB_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.trB_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L147-L147","doc":"The `B`-slot scalar is non-zero, so the ratio is defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.hecke_σ₅","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.hecke_σ₅","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L145-L145","doc":"Hecke relation `σ₅² = (q − q⁻¹) σ₅ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.hecke_σ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.hecke_σ₁","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L143-L143","doc":"Hecke relation `σ₁² = (q − q⁻¹) σ₁ + 1` (AGENTS.md §7a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.eB_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.eB_idem","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Hoefsmit cell content: `e_B⁺` is a projector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.eW_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.eW_idem","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Hoefsmit cell content: `e_W⁺` is a projector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.trM_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.trM_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L137-L137","doc":"Markov-trace cyclicity `tr_M(ab) = tr_M(ba)` — the linking-operation\ninput (`conj:categorical-linking-operation`, Property 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeinbergAngleCategorical","kind":"class","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L100-L150","doc":"**Conjecture carrier (primary, content-bearing, NO instance).**\n\n`WeinbergAngleCategorical R q A d cotW` asserts that the Standard\nModel Weinberg angle is the Hecke-eigenvalue ratio of the two\nelectroweak Hoefsmit-projector traces at `n = 6`:\n\n    cot θ_W · tr_M(e_B⁺ · σ₅⁸) = tr_M(e_W⁺ · σ₁⁴),\n\ni.e. `cot θ_W = trW / trB` (`cot_identification`), where the data `d`\nis the genuine Hecke data — `trM` cyclic (the substrate-side input\nthat `conj:categorical-linking-operation` needs), `eW`, `eB`\nidempotent (Hoefsmit cell content), and `σ₁`, `σ₅` satisfying the\nHecke relation at the substrate parameter `q`.\n\n**What is and is not encoded.**  The pure-pattern evaluation of the\nratio, `cot θ_W = q⁻⁴`, and its comparison against CODATA are the\narchimedean evaluation at the comparison boundary; they live in the\n`.md`, not here.  The Higgs-vev automorphism of the Hoefsmit\ndecomposition (the `(W³, B) ↦ (Z, γ)` rotation, which is what makes\nthe ratio *this* ratio) is **not** formalised — a trace-preserving\nautomorphism exists trivially (`id`), so an existential field would\ncarry no content (the Round-11 trap, `ConditionalClasses.lean`); it\nis recorded as a GAP bean instead.\n\n**Tower status (owner ruling 2026-09-03): ORDER-ZERO-ONLY.**  This\ncarrier is a single Hecke-eigenvalue ratio at fixed `n = 6`; the\nfull-tower derivation (all `n`, all orders in `q`) is not attempted.\n\nNo instance is provided; supplying one asserts the conjecture. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:weinberg-angle-categorical","label":"conj:weinberg-angle-categorical","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg_add_sinSqWeinberg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg_add_sinSqWeinberg","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L89-L96","doc":"The two categorical scalars are a genuine `(cos², sin²)` pair whenever\nthe normalisation `trW² + trB²` is non-zero.  Generic over any field\n(§7c): no ordering, no `Real.sqrt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sinSqWeinberg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sinSqWeinberg","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L85-L87","doc":"`sin² θ_W` as a categorical scalar (see `cosSqWeinberg`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cosSqWeinberg","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L78-L83","doc":"`cos² θ_W` as a categorical scalar.  The `.md` defines\n`cos θ_W = trW / √(trW² + trB²)`; over a generic coefficient field the\nsquare root is not available, so the categorical scalars are the\n**squares** — which is all that `sin² θ_W` (the observable) needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trB","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L69-L70","doc":"`tr_M(e_B⁺ · σ₅⁸)` — the pre-EWSB `B`-slot trace scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trW","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L66-L67","doc":"`tr_M(e_W⁺ · σ₁⁴)` — the `W`-slot trace scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.σ₅","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.σ₅","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Braid generator `σ₅` (the `H`/pre-mixing `B` slot carries `σ₅⁸`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.σ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.σ₁","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Braid generator `σ₁` (the `W` slot carries `σ₁⁴`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.eB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.eB","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Hoefsmit idempotent `e_B⁺` — symmetric channel of the pre-EWSB `B` slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.eW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.eW","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Hoefsmit idempotent `e_W⁺` — symmetric channel of the `W` slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.trM","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The Markov trace `tr_M : A → R` (an `R`-linear functional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWHoefsmitData","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/weinberg-angle-categorical.lean#L39-L60","doc":"**The Hecke-eigenvalue data of the electroweak triplet at `n = 6`**\n(`weinberg-angle-categorical.md`, statement).  A substrate algebra\n`A` over the coefficient ring `R` (intended: `H₆(q) ⊆ End_R(V^{⊗6})`),\nan `R`-linear trace functional `trM` (intended: the Markov trace),\nthe two Hoefsmit idempotents `eW`, `eB` on the symmetric channels of\nthe `W` slot and the pre-EWSB `B` slot, and the two braid generators\n`σ₁`, `σ₅` under the cell-content identification `W ↔ σ₁⁴`,\n`Z ↔ σ₃⁶`, `H/B ↔ σ₅⁸`.\n\nThe structure only *names* the data.  Which of its inhabitants are\nthe physical ones is what the conjecture class below asserts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}